    "response": "{\"decision\":\"established_flaw\",\"issues\":[{\"category\":\"contextual_flattening\",\"target_kind\":\"assertion\",\"claim_quote\":\"Every displayed source presents the same severe and unresolved version of policy debate.\",\"evidence\":[{\"excerpt_id\":\"EXC_8bf6c5caee9df6da\",\"quote\":\"Will my right hon. Friend explain from which budget the fines and compensation will be paid? Is it not perverse that the budget that should be paying for these very improvements is to be used to compensate the companies that have been inconvenienced? Will my right hon. Friend look very closely at the way in which the Office of Rail Regulation has operated since the changes were...\"},{\"excerpt_id\":\"EXC_e36856910070c89f\",\"quote\":\"I think that the ORR does a good job in holding Network Rail to account, but I will of course take seriously what my hon. Friend has said about its performance. If she wants to send me further details of her complaints, I will certainly consider them.\"},{\"excerpt_id\":\"EXC_c54a69daf6a2b9bd\",\"quote\":\"As the Member who represents Finsbury Park, may I ask the Secretary of State to say a big thank you to all the staff who coped with an utterly impossible position on Saturday 27 December, when the station was so overcrowded with passengers? They deserve our recognition and thanks for the hard work that they do The Secretary of State will recall that we had a meeting in his office…\"},{\"excerpt_id\":\"EXC_625975220bf004b2\",\"quote\":\"I join the hon. Gentleman in thanking all the people who were involved in ensuring that the vast majority of the vast number of people who turned up at Finsbury Park were kept as informed as possible, in extremely difficult circumstances. This is certainly one of the issues in which I intend to take a further interest, and I shall be more than happy to meet the hon. Gentleman…\"}],\"whole_packet_no_support\":\"whole_packet_no_support\",\"mechanism\":\"The evidence presents distinct accounts of the Finsbury Park station situation, reflecting different speaker contexts, concerns, and perspectives.\",\"material_consequence\":\"The claim falsely presents a monolithic view of policy debate, ignoring the diverse and specific issues raised across the sources.\",\"counterconditions\":\"The sources represent varied viewpoints and concerns, demonstrating a lack of a single, universally accepted 'severe and unresolved version' of the debate.\"}],\"unresolved\":[],\"rationale\":\"The evidence demonstrates that the claim is a contextual flattening, failing to acknowledge the diverse perspectives and specific concerns presented within the supplied sources. The sources do not present a single, 'severe and unresolved version' of policy debate.\"}",
    "done": true,
    "done_reason": "stop",
